# Everything here is OPTIONAL. The server runs with no .env at all:
#   cd mcp-server && npm start
# Unpinned, /sync accepts any chrome-extension:// origin and rejects every
# web page — which is the threat that actually matters, since a browser sets
# Origin itself and page script cannot forge it.
#
# Pin one extension only if you want to stop *other installed extensions*
# from writing to your queue. It buys nothing against a non-browser local
# process, which can forge any Origin header it likes.
#
# The id is per-machine and per-checkout for an unpacked extension, so there
# is no correct value to share: read yours off chrome://extensions with
# Developer mode on, after loading extension/ unpacked. A STALE value is
# worse than none — the server starts fine, rejects every push, and the
# extension swallows the failure by design, so annotations silently stop
# appearing. Check the server log for "/sync rejected" if that happens.
#
# Once SpotCheck is published to the Web Store, set PUBLISHED_EXTENSION_ORIGIN
# in server.js instead — a published id is fixed and public, so every user
# gets exact-origin matching with no setup.
#
# SPOTCHECK_EXTENSION_ORIGIN=chrome-extension://<your-extension-id>
